## Render cost, offscreen EGL on D3D12 (scratch benchmark, frame time per mjr_render)
line.loader_a.dev.xml: 1600x1000 default 56 ms (17.7 fps); shadows off 26 ms; 800x500 default 61 ms
line.dev.xml:          1600x1000 default 254 ms (3.9 fps); shadows off 97 ms; shadows+reflections off 86 ms; 800x500 259 ms
llvmpipe (software) for comparison: line.dev.xml default 73 ms, loader_a default 37 ms
-> resolution-independent: per-draw-call overhead in Mesa's D3D12 translation layer; the 4096
   shadow map pass roughly doubles it.
## Cause
Physics is 40-120x faster than real time headless. 4.9% real time = 0.002 s timestep x ~25 frames/s:
the viewer advanced one physics step per rendered frame, and a frame costs ~40-60 ms on D3D12
(~250 ms for the full line). Rendering-only: no MJCF change for it (KNOWN_ISSUES).
Separate bug found by the moving benchmark: Euler + PLACEHOLDER actuator damping on the light J4
shaft (inertia ~1.6e-4 kg m^2) diverges (mjWARN_BADQACC at DOF 3 within 4 ms) -> gen_mjcf.py now
sets integrator implicitfast (3.12-compatible, gate OK).
## Fix
tools/view_mjcf.py (M1.6) steps physics to the wall clock (as many mj_step per frame as needed,
frames capped at 60 Hz) and turns shadows off in memory by default (--shadows to keep them).
